WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.379
Many IaC workflows use state to map code
to real infrastructure.

2
00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:13.317
State can contain resource identifiers,
configuration values, outputs,

3
00:00:13.397 --> 00:00:20.909
endpoints, dependencies, relationships,
and sometimes secret-adjacent data.

4
00:00:20.989 --> 00:00:25.888
Even when state does not contain a direct
credential,

5
00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:33.044
it can reveal enough about the environment
to be sensitive operational data.

6
00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:37.697
State storage should be protected
deliberately.

7
00:00:37.777 --> 00:00:42.458
Remote state backends should use access
controls,

8
00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:47.546
encryption where appropriate, locking,
versioning,

9
00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:51.980
and audit logs when the platform supports
them.

10
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.197
Locking helps prevent overlapping changes.

11
00:00:56.277 --> 00:01:00.305
Versioning can help recover from mistakes.

12
00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:07.026
Auditability helps teams understand who
read or changed state and when.

13
00:01:07.106 --> 00:01:14.400
Plans are also security-relevant because
they show what automation intends to

14
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.242
change.

15
00:01:15.322 --> 00:01:21.310
A plan can reveal replacements, deletions,
permission changes,

16
00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:28.466
public exposure, encryption changes,
logging changes, resource movement,

17
00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:30.941
or drift reconciliation.

18
00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:38.751
Reviewing a plan before a high-impact
apply helps teams catch surprises while there

19
00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.790
is still time to stop.

20
00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:45.443
A safe workflow avoids blind production
applies.

21
00:01:45.523 --> 00:01:51.837
Reviewers should understand the intended
change, the environment,

22
00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:57.687
the identity that will apply it, and the
risky parts of the plan.

23
00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:05.279
When drift exists, reconciliation should
be controlled rather than automatic in

24
00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:07.754
sensitive environments.

25
00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:14.910
State and plans together provide
visibility: what exists, what will change,

26
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:19.780
and whether the change matches the
approved intent.
